= A Summer of Protest

A police officer kneels on George Floyd's neck for nine minutes. The video spreads worldwide. Protests fill cities for weeks. Most are peaceful. Some end in looting and burning. A slogan about defunding the police dominates the debate.

- @reform: Back structural police reform.
- @defund: Embrace the slogan.
- @distance: Distance the party from "defund".

@reform
subtitle: Concrete, can pass.
on-arrival: police_reform = 1; enthusiasm += 3; prog_dissent -= 3; mod_dissent += 2; pop_mod -= 0.05

We write the legislation. The details are hard.

@defund
subtitle: The base cheers. Suburbs flinch.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 5; prog_dissent -= 5; mod_dissent += 5; pop_mod -= 0.5; far_left += 3

The slogan is more popular on social media than it is at the ballot box.

@distance
subtitle: Wedge.
on-arrival: mod_dissent -= 4; prog_dissent += 5; pop_mod += 0.2; enthusiasm -= 2

We say reform, not abolition. Activists are unsatisfied.
